1
00:00:01,474 --> 00:00:05,440
Today's trick: the "wheel walk".

2
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:15,713
[Music]

3
00:00:15,713 --> 00:00:20,981
This trick is fairly complicated,
because everything you're used to changes.

4
00:00:21,047 --> 00:00:23,818
In other words, you don't sit
over the wheel in the same way,

5
00:00:23,918 --> 00:00:26,350
and instead of driving the wheel
with the pedals,

6
00:00:26,416 --> 00:00:29,618
you push it directly,
with your feet on the tire.

7
00:00:29,691 --> 00:00:30,809
That changes a lot,

8
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:34,450
which is why it takes
plenty of time and practice. Good luck.

9
00:00:36,261 --> 00:00:38,821
To work on this trick, you have no choice:

10
00:00:38,861 --> 00:00:42,754
you have to hold on to a wall, a railing,
a bar, anything, but hold on!

11
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:45,639
One really important thing
when you're working on the "wheel walk":

12
00:00:45,838 --> 00:00:49,330
if the wheel ends up
shooting out in front of you...

13
00:00:49,670 --> 00:00:52,461
If it goes out behind you, no big deal,
you'll land on your feet.

14
00:00:52,527 --> 00:00:55,288
But if it goes out in front,
remember to spread your feet

15
00:00:55,354 --> 00:00:58,517
so the pedal doesn't catch your calf,
or you can fall backward,

16
00:00:58,583 --> 00:01:00,230
and that's really not pleasant.

17
00:01:04,793 --> 00:01:07,048
So there are several steps
to put together properly.

18
00:01:07,114 --> 00:01:09,382
The first step,
probably the most important one,

19
00:01:09,435 --> 00:01:12,580
is placing your feet correctly
on the tire.

20
00:01:14,307 --> 00:01:17,608
Your feet go parallel to the wheel.

21
00:01:17,674 --> 00:01:18,674
Definitely not duck-footed.

22
00:01:19,087 --> 00:01:22,922
First, you put your toes down,
then slide all the way back to the heel.

23
00:01:22,988 --> 00:01:25,684
My toes go near the frame,

24
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:29,267
my heel goes past the side of the frame,
and I slide it in line with the wheel.

25
00:01:29,787 --> 00:01:31,799
Never point them out like a duck,

26
00:01:32,038 --> 00:01:35,420
and never put one foot
on top of the other, like this.

27
00:01:36,077 --> 00:01:38,872
So I hold on, I put my toes down,

28
00:01:39,471 --> 00:01:42,160
I start moving forward,
keeping well in line with the wheel,

29
00:01:42,226 --> 00:01:46,420
and as soon as there's room here,
see, I put my second foot down.

30
00:01:46,486 --> 00:01:48,249
And so on...

31
00:01:48,315 --> 00:01:49,715
And so on...

32
00:01:49,781 --> 00:01:51,808
And so on...

33
00:01:51,874 --> 00:01:55,926
So first, the really important thing
is that I hold on and make sure

34
00:01:55,979 --> 00:01:58,136
I put my feet on the wheel
toes first, every time,

35
00:01:58,302 --> 00:02:02,297
and as soon as there's room
for the toes of my other foot,

36
00:02:02,363 --> 00:02:03,860
I put them down, and so on.

37
00:02:04,753 --> 00:02:11,087
[Music]

38
00:02:11,087 --> 00:02:12,789
Once your feet are in place,

39
00:02:12,975 --> 00:02:15,430
the second point,
maybe the trickiest one,

40
00:02:15,843 --> 00:02:20,362
is to sit a little further back
relative to the wheel.

41
00:02:20,428 --> 00:02:22,694
Normally, you sit right over the wheel.

42
00:02:22,753 --> 00:02:25,242
Here, the fork
is a little further back,

43
00:02:25,614 --> 00:02:28,020
and the wheel
a little out in front of you.

44
00:02:28,086 --> 00:02:38,641
[Music]

45
00:02:38,641 --> 00:02:40,427
That's what makes this trick so hard.

46
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:43,277
If my saddle and fork
are right above the wheel,

47
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:44,980
I'll always fall forward.

48
00:02:49,808 --> 00:02:54,428
So you really have to find
the position where you sit back

49
00:02:54,494 --> 00:02:59,550
and let the wheel roll
a little ahead, so you're well placed.

50
00:02:59,616 --> 00:03:09,694
[Music]

51
00:03:09,694 --> 00:03:11,771
Getting into the trick
isn't that complicated,

52
00:03:11,837 --> 00:03:13,173
it's a bit like "one foot".

53
00:03:13,286 --> 00:03:15,670
As my foot on the pedal
comes up here,

54
00:03:15,736 --> 00:03:18,580
at the very last moment,
I grab the tire.

55
00:03:18,646 --> 00:03:26,821
[Music]

56
00:03:26,821 --> 00:03:28,900
Getting back on the pedals
is a bit more complicated.

57
00:03:28,966 --> 00:03:30,361
You can look at the pedal.

58
00:03:30,427 --> 00:03:32,210
I don't recommend it, but you can.

59
00:03:36,361 --> 00:03:39,652
You can also hold your foot in the air,
a bit high, above the pedal,

60
00:03:39,718 --> 00:03:43,067
so the pedal touches it
when it reaches the top of its turn.

61
00:03:43,133 --> 00:03:47,402
That lets you feel it, and from there,
all you need is one last push on the tire

62
00:03:47,579 --> 00:03:50,760
with your other foot,
and you can finally ride off again.

63
00:03:55,014 --> 00:03:58,042
If you don't feel the pedal,

64
00:03:58,066 --> 00:04:01,740
switch
to a sort of "one-foot wheel walk".

65
00:04:07,614 --> 00:04:10,332
You can push the wheel
a few times if you need to.

66
00:04:10,832 --> 00:04:12,516
That's actually good,
it's training for "one foot".

67
00:04:12,615 --> 00:04:15,646
And you can even get
a bit of a feel for the "glide" too.

68
00:04:15,712 --> 00:04:17,251
Putting your second foot

69
00:04:17,303 --> 00:04:20,758
on the second pedal isn't hard,
since you already know

70
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:23,748
where one pedal is relative to the other
when one foot is already on.

71
00:04:23,814 --> 00:04:26,029
One last way to do it,
once you've had a bit of practice,

72
00:04:26,095 --> 00:04:30,778
is to put your foot just about anywhere,
and you end up catching it anyway.

73
00:04:30,844 --> 00:04:33,290
But that only comes later.

74
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:42,948
[Music]

75
00:04:42,948 --> 00:04:44,678
Again, this isn't an easy trick.

76
00:04:44,744 --> 00:04:45,822
But it's the trick

77
00:04:45,888 --> 00:04:48,230
that really gets you started
in the world of freestyle.

78
00:04:48,424 --> 00:04:50,164
So hang in there.

79
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:53,603
Don't be put off, it'll take time,
but once you're comfortable

80
00:04:53,636 --> 00:04:57,362
with the "wheel walk",
it opens up a huge range of tricks,

81
00:04:57,408 --> 00:04:59,543
because there are lots
of other "wheel walks" out there.

82
00:04:59,609 --> 00:05:25,170
[Music]
